From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: locality, references, variations, axis ranges, matching by axes, expiration events, number substitution

DirectWrite stubs, as documented now:

- Locality: every font here is on this machine: IsCharacterLocal,
  IsGlyphLocal, AreCharactersLocal and AreGlyphsLocal say so (they said
  FALSE or E_NOTIMPL), GetLocality and GetFontLocality are LOCAL without a
  FIXME, and the download requests have nothing to do (S_OK).
- Font face references (of a face, and IDWriteFontFaceReference1):
  GetFileSize and GetLocalFileSize from the file's stream (they were 0),
  GetFileTime its last write time, Equals (was E_NOTIMPL as a BOOL) the
  same file, index and simulations.
- Variations: HasVariations on faces and resources (always FALSE) is true
  for a font whose fvar axes vary; such axes get
  DWRITE_FONT_AXIS_ATTRIBUTES_VARIABLE (a FIXME), and a font without fvar
  has its four static axes (weight, width, italic, slant), as Windows
  reports them. IDWriteFontFace5::GetFontAxisValueCount/GetFontAxisValues
  give the face's (default instance) axis values.
- Font sets: GetFontAxisRanges for a font and for the set,
  GetFilteredFontIndices and GetFilteredFonts by axis ranges (any or all),
  GetFontSourceType (per machine for the Fonts folder, per user for the
  user's fonts), the source name (empty: no package or provider).
- IDWriteFontFamily2 and IDWriteFontCollection2::GetMatchingFonts by axis
  values (E_NOTIMPL): the values as weight, stretch and style.
- A font list's GetFont gave the family's font at that index, not the
  list's: matching lists came back unsorted; they come in order of the
  match now.
- GetExpirationEvent on collections and font sets (NULL): an event of the
  object's own, not set while it lives.
- AnalyzeNumberSubstitution (a FIXME): the source's number substitution
  runs, their spans of digits told to the sink.

Wine's dwrite font test's 4 expiration-event todos pass.

Gate: test/dwritemisc-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/dwritemisc-probe.c; a
variable font from the host when there is one). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_VARIATIONS, SG_MUTANT_NO_EXPIRATION_EVENT (dwrite/font.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_NUMBER_SUBST (dwrite/analyzer.c).
